      },
      "writtenOn": "2019-06-25T23:11:26Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "For reference, I believe the ANX chip on Eve only has ~9 write cycles before the chip is no longer able to update. This isn\u0027t something we can put in faft, at least for that device.\n\nThe way Karthik defined the meaning for 0 and 1, a FAFT test can get information for 0 and for 1 and compare the two. One will be live data (1) and the other will have the hard coded value (0). FAFT can assert that the values are the same",
      "parentUuid": "ebe58c51_c277684f",
